  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The retail price of a particular model of cell phone, at Jordan's Electronics, is \n$C$ dollars and the purchaser also has to pay an $11%$  tax.\n\nWhich expression represents the total cost, in dollars, of the cell phone after tax is applied?",
  "worked_solution": "The price of the cell phone before taxes is $C$ dollars.\n\nThe amount of tax the purchaser has to pay is $11%$ of the price of a phone or $0.11C$ dollars.\n\nTherefore, the expression that represents the total cost (in dollars) of the cell phone after tax is:\n\n \n\n$$\nC+0.11C.\n$$",
